{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nA related-material pin can be rejected as stale solely because the fingerprint algorithm changed, even though the related ticket's material did not. Historical pin 6b113a084820af9d exactly matches the post-330c/pre-2be7 recomputation of the current prerequisite, while the latest generation yields bbe91c054a677441.\n\n## Proven root cause\n\n`pin_health.derive_health` compares pins only with the latest fingerprint. The plan-review wrapper supplies no compatibility check, although `attest._legacy_material_ok` already recognizes both supported historical full-hash generations for the subject's own material. The prerequisite had no post-review events; wrong-target and genuine-material-drift rivals were rejected. An unmatched hash control remains stale.\n\nOriginal epic `jira-reb-1160` defines actual related-material drift as the invalidation boundary. Story `convulsive-calx-yearling` requires recovery when review-time related material remains current. `ethnogenic-forbidden-umbrette` requires genuine dependency edits to invalidate unconditionally.\n\n## Repair plan\n\n- Extend related-pin health with a narrowly scoped compatibility predicate supplied by the attestation layer.\n- Classify a mismatched latest fingerprint as current only when recomputing the current related ticket under a supported historical full-fingerprint generation exactly matches the signed pin.\n- Preserve current-fingerprint reporting, malformed/missing classifications, enforcement semantics, and genuine unmatched drift.\n- Add a held-out ephemeral-store unit oracle at the real attestation-to-pin-health seam.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Run `pytest tests/unit/test_plan_material_pin_generation_3e0f.py tests/unit/test_plan_material_pin_health.py tests/unit/test_plan_material_pin_health_heldout.py`.\n- Run `make lint` and `make typecheck`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] An unchanged related ticket pinned with the post-330c/pre-2be7 fingerprint is classified current, checked by `pytest tests/unit/test_plan_material_pin_generation_3e0f.py`.\n- [ ] A semantic edit makes that same historical pin stale, checked by `pytest tests/unit/test_plan_material_pin_generation_3e0f.py`.\n- [ ] An arbitrary unmatched valid hash remains stale, checked by `pytest tests/unit/test_plan_material_pin_generation_3e0f.py`.\n- [ ] Latest-generation, malformed, missing, advisory, and enforced health behavior remains compatible, checked by the focused pin-health suite.\n- [ ] The held-out oracle is RED before the fix, GREEN after the fix, and RED again when historical compatibility is removed."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786298824669834001,"uuid":"8b699e96-01c6-4a76-a398-9ab1c425b4e7"}